# WHY this file is the real gate. Everything else that keeps this tree honest —
# the test suite, the byte pins in tests/helpers/boundary-locks.mjs, the
# structure gates — lives in files an automated agent can edit in the same breath
# as the code those gates judge. gates.lock makes that tampering loud instead of
# silent, but loud is not prevented. THIS is what prevents it: with branch
# protection on main, a change to any path below needs a human approver, and no
# agent can grant itself that right or take it away.
#
# If you are setting this repository up, enable branch protection on `main` and
# require at least one approving review on these paths. Without that setting,
# this file is a suggestion and gates.lock is the only thing standing between an
# agent and a green check that means nothing.

# The acceptance surface itself, named so it can never fall through to the
# catch-all. tests/ and scripts/ are deliberately NOT wildcarded: an agent that
# only ever edits a gate can weaken the gate and the tree at the same time, and
# these are exactly the paths where that is possible.

tests/
scripts/
gates.lock

# The verifier. It cannot pin its own hash, so this entry is its only guard.

/scripts/gates.mjs

